QUERY PARAMETER:
*query parameters are values passed after ? in the URL.
*Query Parameters These appear after a ? in the URL and are used for filtering, sorting, searching, or pagination. They are optional and do not change the identity of the resource. Example:
    GET /cars?color=blue&brand=ferrari

PARAMETER VALIDATION
*It is possible to apply validation conditions on path parameters as well as query parameters of the URL
*In order to apply the validation conditions on a path parameter, you need to import the Path class. In addition to the default value of the parameter, you can specify the maximum and minimum length in the case of a string parameter.
from fastapi import FastAPI,Path
import uvicorn

app=FastAPI()

@app.get("/validation/{name}")
async def fun(name:str=Path(...,min_length=3,max_length=10)):
    return {"name":name}

if __name__ == "__main__":
   uvicorn.run("parameter_validation:app", host="127.0.0.1", port=8080, reload=True)


